Chapter: ApplyAnnotationsScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 Generates apply-annotations.ps1, phase two of two. It reads the report
 phase one wrote and a human then edited, and it is the only half that
 mutates anything.

 Every block carries its source VERBATIM in the report, and a block whose
 lines no longer match the file is refused. The refusal is per FILE, not
 per block: a report written against an older tree is stale everywhere in
 that file at once, and applying the blocks that still happen to match
 would cut the right lines out of the wrong places. A stale report must be
 a refusal rather than a corruption, because the corruption is silent and
 spread across thousands of chapters.

 Nothing is written without -Apply. Without it the run verifies every
 block and prints what it would do, which is the mode to trust after
 editing the report.

 Keep the definition count low; see the note in ExtractAnnotationsScript
 for what happens to the CHECK deck otherwise.

 We say:

Section: Parameters

  apply-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-optional "Report" SptString, sh-param-optional "Only" SptString, sh-param-optional "Author" SptString, sh-switch "Apply", sh-switch "List"]

Section: S01 -- Preamble

 The header line is file, line range, target, verdict and signals. The
 verdict is one or two words, so it is captured whole and split after.

  head-pattern : Text = "^@@ (.+?) \\| ([0-9]+)-([0-9]+) \\| (.+?) \\| (.+?) \\| (.*)$"

  s01 : List ShellCmd = [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, ScAssign "Repo" (SePathResolve (SePathJoin SeScriptRoot (SeLit ".."))), ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "Report")) [ScAssign "Report" (SePathJoin (SeVar "Repo") (SeLit "docs\\Reports\\AnnotationExtract.txt"))] [ScAssign "Report" (SeStaticCall "System.IO.Path" "GetFullPath" [SeVar "Report"])], ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "Author")) [ScAssign "Author" (SeLit "blu")] [], ScAssign "HeadPat" (SeLit head-pattern), ScAssign "today" (SeFormatTime SeNow "yyyy-MM-dd"), ScBlank, ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "Report"))) [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeLit "no report at ") (SeVar "Report")), ScExit (SeInt 2)] [], ScAssign "script:recs" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.List[object]" "new" []), ScAssign "script:staleFiles" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "script:cutBlocks" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "script:cutLines" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "script:annWritten" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "script:filesChanged" (SeInt 0)]

Section: S02 -- Parse-Report

 A record is finalised when the next header arrives or the file ends, so
 the flush is written once and called from both places.

  flush-cmds : List ShellCmd = [ScIf (SeVar "curFile") [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "script:recs") "Add" [SeOrderedMap [SfField "file" (SeVar "curFile"), SfField "start" (SeVar "curStart"), SfField "stop" (SeVar "curStop"), SfField "target" (SeVar "curTarget"), SfField "verb" (SeVar "curVerb"), SfField "kind" (SeVar "curKind"), SfField "body" (SeVar "curBody")]])] []]

  parse-head : List ShellCmd = [ScSequence flush-cmds, ScAssign "curFile" (SeIndex (SeVar "matches") (SeInt 1)), ScAssign "curStart" (SeCast "int" (SeIndex (SeVar "matches") (SeInt 2))), ScAssign "curStop" (SeCast "int" (SeIndex (SeVar "matches") (SeInt 3))), ScAssign "curTarget" (SeIndex (SeVar "matches") (SeInt 4)), ScAssign "vfull" (SeTrim (SeIndex (SeVar "matches") (SeInt 5))), ScAssign "vparts" (SeSplit (SeVar "vfull") " "), ScAssign "curVerb" (SeIndex (SeVar "vparts") (SeInt 0)), ScAssign "curKind" (SeIfElse (SeIntGt (SeCount (SeVar "vparts")) (SeInt 1)) (SeIndex (SeVar "vparts") (SeInt 1)) (SeLit "rationale")), ScAssign "curBody" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.List[string]" "new" [])]

  s02 : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "curFile" (SeLit ""), ScAssign "curStart" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "curStop" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "curTarget" (SeLit ""), ScAssign "curVerb" (SeLit ""), ScAssign "curKind" (SeLit ""), ScAssign "curBody" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.List[string]" "new" []), ScForEach "rl" (SeStaticCall "System.IO.File" "ReadAllLines" [SeVar "Report"]) [ScIf (SeMatchExpr (SeVar "rl") (SeVar "HeadPat")) [ScSequence parse-head, ScContinue] [], ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "rl") (SeLit "> ")) [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "curBody") "Add" [SeSubstringFrom (SeVar "rl") (SeInt 2)])] []], ScSequence flush-cmds, ScEcho (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "report: ") (SeCount (SeVar "script:recs"))) (SeLit " records"))]

Section: S03 -- Apply-File

 Verify first, mutate second, and never interleave the two: a file is
 either wholly consistent with the report or wholly refused.

  json-body : ShellExpr = SeReplace (SeReplace (SeReplace (SeTrim (SeJoin (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "body") (SeLit " "))) "\\s+" (SeLit " ")) "\\\\" (SeLit "\\\\")) "\"" (SeLit "\\\"")

  ann-record : ShellExpr = SeLines [SeLit "  {", SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    \"target\": \"") (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "target")) (SeLit "\","), SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    \"kind\": \"") (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "kind")) (SeLit "\","), SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    \"author\": \"") (SeVar "Author")) (SeLit "\","), SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    \"date\": \"") (SeVar "today")) (SeLit "\","), SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "    \"body\": \"") json-body) (SeLit "\","), SeLit "    \"thread\": null", SeLit "  }"]

  verify-cmds : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "ok" (SeBool True), ScAssign "x" (SeInt 0), ScWhile (SeAnd (SeIntLt (SeVar "x") (SeCount (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "body"))) (SeVar "ok")) [ScAssign "idx" (SeSub (SeAdd (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "start") (SeVar "x")) (SeInt 1)), ScIf (SeIntGe (SeVar "idx") (SeCount (SeVar "lines"))) [ScAssign "ok" (SeBool False)] [ScIf (SeStringNeq (SeIndex (SeVar "lines") (SeVar "idx")) (SeIndex (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "body") (SeVar "x"))) [ScAssign "ok" (SeBool False)] []], ScIncrement "x"]]

  collect-cmds : List ShellCmd = [ScSequence verify-cmds, ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "ok")) [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "  STALE ") (SeVar "f")) (SeLit " line ")) (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "start")), ScAssign "stale" (SeBool True), ScContinue] [], ScIf (SeStringEq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "verb") (SeLit "KEEP")) [ScContinue] [], ScAssign "x" (SeInt 0), ScWhile (SeIntLt (SeVar "x") (SeCount (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "body"))) [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "del") "Add" [SeSub (SeAdd (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "start") (SeVar "x")) (SeInt 1)]), ScIncrement "x"], ScIf (SeStringEq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "verb") (SeLit "ANNOTATE")) [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "anns") "Add" [ann-record])] []]

 A removed block leaves the blank line above it and the blank line below,
 so runs of blanks are collapsed to one. Without this every extraction
 leaves a widening gap behind it.

  keep-line : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "ln" (SeIndex (SeVar "lines") (SeVar "x")), ScIf (SeStringEq (SeTrim (SeVar "ln")) (SeLit "")) [ScIncrement "blank"] [ScAssign "blank" (SeInt 0)], ScIf (SeIntLe (SeVar "blank") (SeInt 1)) [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "kept") "Add" [SeVar "ln"])] []]

  rebuild-cmds : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "kept" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.List[string]" "new" []), ScAssign "blank" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "x" (SeInt 0), ScWhile (SeIntLt (SeVar "x") (SeCount (SeVar "lines"))) [ScIf (SeNot (SeMethodCall (SeVar "del") "Contains" [SeVar "x"])) keep-line [], ScIncrement "x"]]

  sidecar-cmds : List ShellCmd = [ScAssign "side" (SePathJoin (SeVar "Repo") (SePathJoin (SeLit "annotations") (SeReplace (SeVar "f") "\\.codex$" (SeLit ".json")))), ScAssign "prior" (SeLit ""), ScIf (SeFileExists (SeVar "side")) [ScAssign "prior" (SeTrim (SeReplace (SeReplace (SeStaticCall "System.IO.File" "ReadAllText" [SeVar "side"]) "^\\s*\\[" (SeLit "")) "\\]\\s*$" (SeLit "")))] [], ScAssign "joined" (SeJoin (SeVar "anns") (SeLit ",\n")), ScIf (SeVar "prior") [ScAssign "joined" (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeVar "prior") (SeLit ",\n")) (SeVar "joined"))] [], ScMkdir (SePathParent (SeVar "side")), ScSetContent (SeVar "side") (SeLines [SeLit "[", SeVar "joined", SeLit "]"]), ScIncrementBy "script:annWritten" (SeCount (SeVar "anns"))]

  s03 : List ShellCmd = [ScFunction "Apply-File" [sh-param-optional "f" SptString] [ScAssign "full" (SePathJoin (SeVar "Repo") (SeVar "f")), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "full"))) [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeLit "  MISSING ") (SeVar "f")), ScIncrement "script:staleFiles", ScReturn (SeBool False)] [], ScAssign "lines" (SeStaticCall "System.IO.File" "ReadAllLines" [SeVar "full"]), ScAssign "del" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[int]" "new" []), ScAssign "anns" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.List[string]" "new" []), ScAssign "stale" (SeBool False), ScForEach "r" (SeVar "script:recs") [ScIf (SeStringNeq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "file") (SeVar "f")) [ScContinue] [], ScSequence collect-cmds], ScIf (SeVar "stale") [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeLit "  REFUSED (stale report): ") (SeVar "f")), ScIncrement "script:staleFiles", ScReturn (SeBool False)] [], ScIf (SeIntEq (SeCount (SeVar "del")) (SeInt 0)) [ScReturn (SeBool False)] [], ScIncrementBy "script:cutLines" (SeCount (SeVar "del")), ScIncrement "script:filesChanged", ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "Apply")) [ScEcho (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "  would cut ") (SeCount (SeVar "del"))) (SeLit " lines from ")) (SeVar "f")), ScReturn (SeBool True)] [], ScSetWritable (SeVar "full"), ScSequence rebuild-cmds, ScDotNetCall "System.IO.File" "WriteAllLines" [SeVar "full", SeVar "kept"], ScIf (SeIntGt (SeCount (SeVar "anns")) (SeInt 0)) sidecar-cmds [], ScEcho (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "  cut ") (SeCount (SeVar "del"))) (SeLit " lines from ")) (SeVar "f")), ScReturn (SeBool True)]]

Section: S04 -- Main

  s04 : List ShellCmd = [ScSequence s02, ScBlank, ScAssign "fileSet" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[string]" "new" []), ScForEach "r" (SeVar "script:recs") [ScIf (SeStringEq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "verb") (SeLit "KEEP")) [ScContinue] [], ScIf (SeAnd (SeVar "Only") (SeStringNeq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "file") (SeVar "Only"))) [ScContinue] [], ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "fileSet") "Add" [SeProperty (SeVar "r") "file"])], ScIf (SeVar "List") [ScForEach "f" (SeVar "fileSet") [ScEcho (SeVar "f")], ScAssign "sideSet" (SeStaticCall "System.Collections.Generic.HashSet[string]" "new" []), ScForEach "r" (SeVar "script:recs") [ScIf (SeStringNeq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "verb") (SeLit "ANNOTATE")) [ScContinue] [], ScIf (SeAnd (SeVar "Only") (SeStringNeq (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "file") (SeVar "Only"))) [ScContinue] [], ScAssign "sp" (SePathJoin (SeVar "Repo") (SePathJoin (SeLit "annotations") (SeReplace (SeProperty (SeVar "r") "file") "\\.codex$" (SeLit ".json")))), ScIf (SeFileExists (SeVar "sp")) [ScDiscard (SeMethodCall (SeVar "sideSet") "Add" [SeVar "sp"])] []], ScForEach "s" (SeVar "sideSet") [ScEcho (SeVar "s")], ScExit (SeInt 0)] [], ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "Apply")) [ScEcho (SeLit "DRY RUN -- nothing is written. Pass -Apply to mutate.")] [], ScForEach "f" (SeVar "fileSet") [ScDiscard (SeCall "Apply-File" [SeVar "f"])], ScBlank, ScEcho (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit "files ") (SeVar "script:filesChanged")) (SeLit ", lines cut ")) (SeVar "script:cutLines")) (SeConcat (SeConcat (SeLit ", annotations ") (SeVar "script:annWritten")) (SeConcat (SeLit ", refused ") (SeVar "script:staleFiles"))))]

Section: Assembly

  apply-script : ShellScript = sh-script "apply-annotations" "Apply an audited annotation-extraction report: cut prose from source and write the sidecars" apply-params [ScSequence s01, ScBlank, ScSequence s03, ScBlank, ScSequence s04]

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell apply-script)
  end

